1
00:01:52,139 --> 00:01:53,897
5x09 - Pie

2
00:01:58,065 --> 00:01:59,705
Subtitles: sub-way.fr

3
00:02:13,754 --> 00:02:16,471
Rise and shine,
morning glories.

4
00:02:16,591 --> 00:02:18,304
First day of production.

5
00:02:19,683 --> 00:02:20,688
Wake up!

6
00:02:22,701 --> 00:02:24,714
Wake up.
Baby bro starts shooting today.

7
00:02:24,874 --> 00:02:26,440
We all need to be up
to support him.

8
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:27,810
Hell, I'm up!

9
00:02:29,401 --> 00:02:32,106
You are now, son.
Let's go, manager.

10
00:02:33,174 --> 00:02:35,316
Your number-one client
starts shooting today.

11
00:02:35,436 --> 00:02:37,370
- I don't think you want to Miss it.
- Jesus.

12
00:02:37,490 --> 00:02:39,096
Baby bro.
Baby bro.

13
00:02:39,288 --> 00:02:40,558
Yeah, Johnny.

14
00:02:42,476 --> 00:02:43,682
How'd you get down here?

15
00:02:43,802 --> 00:02:45,733
I've been up for hours.
You blew right past me.

16
00:02:45,853 --> 00:02:47,139
- Really?
- Yup.

17
00:02:47,722 --> 00:02:50,156
- Ready for work today?
- Getting there.

18
00:02:50,557 --> 00:02:52,701
You want me to make you
anything special for breakfast?

19
00:02:52,898 --> 00:02:54,761
I'm okay.
I'm not really hungry.

20
00:02:55,430 --> 00:02:56,579
Not hungry?

21
00:03:04,609 --> 00:03:06,609
Hopefully it's just
first day jitters, bro.

22
00:03:06,729 --> 00:03:08,499
Leave him alone.
He's fine.

23
00:03:09,039 --> 00:03:11,340
He barely slept last night,
now he doesn't want to eat.

24
00:03:11,460 --> 00:03:12,571
He's not fine.

25
00:03:13,790 --> 00:03:16,776
- Here, drink a powerade, bro.
- No thanks.

26
00:03:16,896 --> 00:03:19,324
- Get your electrolytes up.
- No thank you.

27
00:03:19,927 --> 00:03:22,605
This is not the best way to start
the most important job of your career.

28
00:03:22,765 --> 00:03:24,972
- You trying to freak him out?
- I'm trying to calm him.

29
00:03:25,092 --> 00:03:26,807
You're not.
You're making us all crazy.

30
00:03:26,927 --> 00:03:29,526
He's not getting crazy.
Vince ain't like us.

31
00:03:29,646 --> 00:03:31,152
He's cool as ice, right?

32
00:03:31,389 --> 00:03:33,033
Actually,
I am a bit nervous.

33
00:03:33,401 --> 00:03:36,103
- God damn it, I knew it.
- Will you shut up, please?

34
00:03:36,571 --> 00:03:38,538
- You shut up.
- What's the problem?

35
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:42,000
I don't know. I just feel a bit off.
I haven't been on a set in over a year.

36
00:03:42,302 --> 00:03:44,275
I's like riding a bike.
You just do what you do.

37
00:03:44,395 --> 00:03:46,671
Verner hasn't had a second
to talk to me about my character.

38
00:03:46,831 --> 00:03:48,435
Can you even understand that guy?

39
00:03:48,555 --> 00:03:50,399
Sounds like a cat
with a german hairball.

40
00:03:50,519 --> 00:03:52,545
The guy's won
two foreign academy awards.

41
00:03:52,665 --> 00:03:54,125
He's a really good director.

42
00:03:54,245 --> 00:03:56,317
- So this is all good?
- It's all good.

43
00:03:56,437 --> 00:03:59,129
- What's your first scene?
- Entering the brush with Jason Patric.

44
00:03:59,249 --> 00:04:00,718
Nice.
I like Jason Patric.

45
00:04:00,838 --> 00:04:04,515
When he was doing <i>Rush</i> he stuck
real needles in his arm to prep.

46
00:04:04,635 --> 00:04:07,817
That's what inspired me to do real coke
when I did the Menendez brothers movie.

47
00:04:08,178 --> 00:04:12,148
- Weren't you an extra on that?
- So? Still kept it real like J.P. does.

48
00:04:12,407 --> 00:04:14,711
- Now you're freaking me out.
- Sorry, bro.

49
00:04:14,831 --> 00:04:17,552
Don't worry about it. It's gonna be
like all the other movies you've done.

50
00:04:17,672 --> 00:04:20,174
- Only a little bit bigger.
- <i>11 and 15, fire.</i>

51
00:04:23,011 --> 00:04:24,485
Six, seven,

52
00:04:24,827 --> 00:04:25,838
fire!

53
00:04:26,068 --> 00:04:28,463
- 22, 24.
- Holy shit.

54
00:04:28,786 --> 00:04:30,673
Fire 45 to 60.

55
00:04:33,428 --> 00:04:35,094
Okay, number 60, fire.

56
00:04:36,497 --> 00:04:38,056
Camera three and two,

57
00:04:38,216 --> 00:04:39,560
closer closer.

58
00:04:39,680 --> 00:04:42,347
Okay, all choppers,
now follow me.

59
00:04:44,264 --> 00:04:46,018
This is gonna be sick.

60
00:04:51,012 --> 00:04:52,372
Any word from the forest?

61
00:04:52,492 --> 00:04:54,509
Vince got his start gift
and he says thank you.

62
00:04:54,629 --> 00:04:56,464
Great.
What did I get him?

63
00:04:56,836 --> 00:04:58,867
A sea salt scrub
from Bliss spa.

64
00:04:59,195 --> 00:05:01,714
- Are you kidding me?
- Yes, of course I am.

65
00:05:01,834 --> 00:05:03,659
You got him a jet ski
for the lake out there.

66
00:05:03,779 --> 00:05:05,605
Great.
I have amazing taste.

67
00:05:05,725 --> 00:05:08,576
Good work, Lloyd.
What's my fortune cookie tell me?

68
00:05:08,696 --> 00:05:11,308
That's you've got lunch
with Andrew Klein and that you cannot...

69
00:05:11,428 --> 00:05:13,222
- Cancel it.
- You cannot cancel it.

70
00:05:13,342 --> 00:05:15,003
I'm the boss.
I can do whatever I want.

71
00:05:15,123 --> 00:05:16,942
You've canceled on him
six times already.

72
00:05:17,062 --> 00:05:19,874
- You can't cancel again.
- I don't want to sit at lunch with him.

73
00:05:19,994 --> 00:05:21,531
- It makes me sad.
- Why?

74
00:05:21,651 --> 00:05:23,620
Because it reminds me
of what I might've become.

75
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:26,748
- A TV lit agent in Encino.
- You did not become that.

76
00:05:26,868 --> 00:05:28,830
So sit at lunch with him
and feel good about that.

77
00:05:28,950 --> 00:05:31,811
You sit at lunch with him
knowing you could be him one day

78
00:05:31,931 --> 00:05:33,820
- if you don't listen to me.
- When do I don't?

79
00:05:34,095 --> 00:05:36,114
Right now
when I'm telling you to cancel it.

80
00:05:36,383 --> 00:05:38,629
Andrew Klein was once
your close friend and mentor.

81
00:05:38,749 --> 00:05:42,362
Now go reminisce and enjoy yourself
because I'm not canceling.

82
00:05:42,872 --> 00:05:44,962
Maybe put on
a cheaper watch though

83
00:05:45,082 --> 00:05:46,806
so he doesn't feel too bad.

84
00:05:50,399 --> 00:05:53,303
Run down to Geary's
and get me a stainless Rolex.

85
00:05:56,757 --> 00:05:58,493
I know what's in there
waiting for me.

86
00:05:58,613 --> 00:06:01,056
And nine other brave souls
knew what was waiting for them.

87
00:06:01,176 --> 00:06:03,057
There's no way I cannot go now.

88
00:06:03,217 --> 00:06:06,267
Maybe...
try it with a little more emotion, bro.

89
00:06:06,387 --> 00:06:08,875
I'm just memorizing,
Johnny, thanks.

90
00:06:09,320 --> 00:06:11,403
Saving it up for in front
of the cameras, right?

91
00:06:12,375 --> 00:06:15,223
- Just checking.
- We're ready for you, Mr. Chase.

92
00:06:18,124 --> 00:06:19,275
Show time.

93
00:06:23,838 --> 00:06:25,942
You know, you did mess up
that one line, though.

94
00:06:26,062 --> 00:06:27,323
- I did?
- Yeah.

95
00:06:27,708 --> 00:06:29,228
You said nine other brave souls

96
00:06:29,348 --> 00:06:31,255
as opposed to the eight
other brave souls.

97
00:06:31,375 --> 00:06:33,118
Oh, right.
Obviously.

98
00:06:33,716 --> 00:06:35,497
Jesus, when do I mess up lines?

99
00:06:35,617 --> 00:06:37,992
Just write the number eight
down on the inside of your palm.

100
00:06:38,112 --> 00:06:40,793
This way you can just sneak a peek.
I do that shit all the time.

101
00:06:40,913 --> 00:06:43,086
Or, who was number eight
on the basketball team?

102
00:06:43,206 --> 00:06:45,313
- You were, Turtle.
- Thank of that.

103
00:06:45,899 --> 00:06:46,940
Good tip.

104
00:06:47,060 --> 00:06:48,803
- Vincent.
- Hey, Verner.

105
00:06:49,908 --> 00:06:51,963
I thought you were
shortening your hair.

106
00:06:52,516 --> 00:06:54,653
- I wasn't told.
- It's fine.

107
00:06:55,225 --> 00:06:57,280
Doesn't matter.
You ready to go?

108
00:06:58,183 --> 00:06:59,704
I'd love a minute to discuss

109
00:06:59,824 --> 00:07:01,658
what you want me to do
with this character.

110
00:07:01,818 --> 00:07:03,553
There's nothing to discuss.
We shoot it.

111
00:07:03,673 --> 00:07:06,861
If I don't like it I will tell you.
But I'm sure I will like it. Okay?

112
00:07:11,638 --> 00:07:13,528
Verner, is this pack
regulation or what?

113
00:07:13,648 --> 00:07:15,501
- Yes, it is.
- Feels light to me.

114
00:07:15,621 --> 00:07:18,003
No, it is the correct
weight, Jason.

115
00:07:19,037 --> 00:07:20,735
Do you know Vincent Chase?

116
00:07:21,221 --> 00:07:23,714
- Not personally. I'm a big fan.
- Yeah, me too.

117
00:07:24,915 --> 00:07:26,094
What do you weigh?

118
00:07:26,689 --> 00:07:27,703
170.

119
00:07:29,759 --> 00:07:31,688
You know, they offered me
that <i>Aquaman 2</i>.

120
00:07:32,003 --> 00:07:33,044
Really?

121
00:07:33,841 --> 00:07:34,905
Not really.

122
00:07:35,374 --> 00:07:38,152
Sequels, water-- come on, my friend.
It's not for me.

123
00:07:38,492 --> 00:07:39,917
Well, me either, I guess.

124
00:07:41,358 --> 00:07:42,536
That's funny.

125
00:07:43,484 --> 00:07:44,659
Okay, let's shoot.

126
00:07:44,981 --> 00:07:48,095
- Aren't we gonna rehearse first?
- No, we shoot the rehearsal.

127
00:07:48,215 --> 00:07:49,219
Love that!

128
00:07:49,749 --> 00:07:51,529
- Break a leg, bro.
- Knock 'em dead.

129
00:07:51,649 --> 00:07:52,959
Cue the fire!

130
00:08:01,744 --> 00:08:03,394
The fire's coming from the west.

131
00:08:03,514 --> 00:08:05,267
The west winds are blowing
out of control.

132
00:08:05,387 --> 00:08:08,725
- We'll have to bring in more men, sir.
- There are no more men to bring in.

133
00:08:12,319 --> 00:08:14,605
You know what's waiting
in there for you.

134
00:08:14,725 --> 00:08:17,453
And eight other brave souls
knew what was waiting for them.

135
00:08:17,573 --> 00:08:19,386
There's no way you can't go now.

136
00:08:19,688 --> 00:08:21,222
- That's Vince's line.
- Cut!

137
00:08:21,342 --> 00:08:23,277
Perfect, let's move on.

138
00:08:23,566 --> 00:08:25,267
- One take?
- Yes!

139
00:08:26,143 --> 00:08:27,376
Love that!

140
00:08:45,965 --> 00:08:47,006
There he is.

141
00:08:47,796 --> 00:08:48,806
Come here.

142
00:08:49,219 --> 00:08:51,246
- How are you, Andrew?
- Pretty good. Pretty good.

143
00:08:51,366 --> 00:08:53,269
God, you look great.

144
00:08:53,429 --> 00:08:55,203
Thank you.
Try to keep healthy.

145
00:08:55,389 --> 00:08:57,107
- You know.
- Yeah, sure.

146
00:08:59,142 --> 00:09:00,902
- Should we sit?
- Oh, yeah, sorry.

147
00:09:01,477 --> 00:09:03,586
These fuckers.
They're not honoring my reservation.

148
00:09:03,706 --> 00:09:05,885
So they're saying a table
is gonna take about 30 minutes.

149
00:09:06,005 --> 00:09:08,158
So I thought we'd just eat
at the bar, if that's okay.

150
00:09:08,278 --> 00:09:09,501
Bar is great.

151
00:09:09,779 --> 00:09:14,041
Barkeeper, can I have another
mccallum 18 neat for my buddy here?

152
00:09:14,315 --> 00:09:16,059
You're still drinking
scotch, I assume?

153
00:09:16,179 --> 00:09:17,959
Not usually for lunch. But...

154
00:09:18,370 --> 00:09:19,834
it's a special occasion.

155
00:09:20,163 --> 00:09:21,862
It's been a long time.

156
00:09:23,853 --> 00:09:26,839
I remember the last time
I had a drink with you

157
00:09:27,113 --> 00:09:28,122
I ended up

158
00:09:28,675 --> 00:09:30,515
covering your boss' phones

159
00:09:30,675 --> 00:09:33,038
while you fucked
that cocktail waitress

160
00:09:33,158 --> 00:09:35,232
you snuck into the mailroom.
Remember that?

161
00:09:35,478 --> 00:09:37,780
I could not believe the sounds
coming out of that room.

162
00:09:37,900 --> 00:09:40,690
Well, you know what?
She did a nice job.

163
00:09:40,992 --> 00:09:42,005
Did she?

164
00:09:42,329 --> 00:09:44,192
I'm so happy for you,
believe me.

165
00:09:44,647 --> 00:09:46,492
You almost got me fired.
You remember that?

166
00:09:46,612 --> 00:09:49,784
You accidentally dropped that
conference call with John ritter.

167
00:09:49,944 --> 00:09:51,661
- No, it was John Goodman.
- Was it?

168
00:09:51,821 --> 00:09:53,361
And I didn't feel badly at all.

169
00:09:53,481 --> 00:09:55,205
I figured maybe
I was doing you a favor.

170
00:09:55,325 --> 00:09:56,931
I love it.
Come here, you dick.

171
00:09:59,053 --> 00:10:01,129
- Oh, man.
- We had some good times.

172
00:10:01,668 --> 00:10:02,672
Too many.

173
00:10:02,832 --> 00:10:05,417
We should not let too much
time pass this time.

174
00:10:06,661 --> 00:10:08,323
No, for sure we shouldn't.

175
00:10:09,874 --> 00:10:11,264
What's wrong?
You all right?

176
00:10:11,384 --> 00:10:12,438
It's just...

177
00:10:13,528 --> 00:10:16,076
This wasn't just a friendly call.

178
00:10:18,172 --> 00:10:19,186
Oh no?

179
00:10:24,057 --> 00:10:25,674
- How was lunch?
- Pricey.

180
00:10:25,794 --> 00:10:28,660
- In Encino?
- He needs a loan, Lloyd.

181
00:10:29,112 --> 00:10:30,112
Half a mil.

182
00:10:30,232 --> 00:10:32,623
Double oy. Well, you don't
have to give it to him.

183
00:10:32,743 --> 00:10:35,116
Yes I do.
Andy and I were once brothers.

184
00:10:35,664 --> 00:10:37,749
A twist of fate turned
one of us into gold

185
00:10:37,869 --> 00:10:39,530
and one of us into,
well, a broke,

186
00:10:39,650 --> 00:10:42,811
desperate,
begging-for-money cocksucker.

187
00:10:43,612 --> 00:10:46,025
- What are those?
- His books. Company books.

188
00:10:46,145 --> 00:10:48,328
He gave them to me to prove
that he could pay me back.

189
00:10:48,448 --> 00:10:50,952
What am I doing? You Asian,
are supposed to be good with numbers.

190
00:10:51,072 --> 00:10:53,629
Figure out if he has any shot
of paying me back.

191
00:10:53,749 --> 00:10:55,985
Because if he doesn't,
you will!

192
00:11:01,276 --> 00:11:02,810
- Maybe it was a mistake.
- Maybe.

193
00:11:02,930 --> 00:11:04,563
Seems like an odd mistake.

194
00:11:04,683 --> 00:11:06,344
The guy does a movie
every five years.

195
00:11:06,464 --> 00:11:09,104
Maybe he's trying to make up
for it by saying extra words.

196
00:11:09,224 --> 00:11:11,262
- You got to talk to him.
- What am I gonna say?

197
00:11:11,382 --> 00:11:14,612
Say, "Hey, Jason, you got a literacy
problem or did you just steal my lines?"

198
00:11:14,732 --> 00:11:17,288
- What if he says I did?
- We may have to get tough with him.

199
00:11:18,458 --> 00:11:21,292
I hear he's like
a fifth-degree black belt.

200
00:11:21,836 --> 00:11:24,046
I'll get tough.
I'm just saying the guy's intense.

201
00:11:24,166 --> 00:11:26,839
All right, relax. No one's getting
tough. I'm sure it was an accident.

202
00:11:26,999 --> 00:11:28,125
A bad accident.

203
00:11:28,245 --> 00:11:32,291
It was a major moment for my character
to say I'm man enough to go into.

204
00:11:32,411 --> 00:11:35,389
- And now I basically bail on it.
- Why didn't the director say anything?

205
00:11:35,549 --> 00:11:38,559
Why didn't anybody say anything?
The script supervisor? Nobody.

206
00:11:38,719 --> 00:11:41,336
'cause it's Jason Patric
and everyone's scared of him.

207
00:11:41,456 --> 00:11:43,538
But Turtle's right.
You got to nip this in the bud.

208
00:11:43,658 --> 00:11:46,007
That's how a star
marks his territory.

209
00:11:46,127 --> 00:11:48,476
Andrew Shue did the same
thing to me on <i>Melrose</i>.

210
00:11:48,596 --> 00:11:51,053
- How'd you stop him?
- I banged his girl.

211
00:11:51,173 --> 00:11:53,985
- What did that do?
- I don't know, but she was booming.

212
00:11:55,187 --> 00:11:56,804
I'm gonna go talk to him.

213
00:11:57,029 --> 00:11:58,386
- Right behind you.
- Alone.

214
00:11:58,506 --> 00:11:59,690
All right. Go get him.

215
00:11:59,810 --> 00:12:02,084
Remind him he got
molested in <i>Sleepers</i>.

216
00:12:02,543 --> 00:12:04,433
That'll throw him off balance.

217
00:12:09,252 --> 00:12:10,258
What?

218
00:12:10,541 --> 00:12:12,260
Yeah, Jason, it's Vince.

219
00:12:14,622 --> 00:12:15,647
Come in.

220
00:12:22,619 --> 00:12:23,914
Everything okay?

221
00:12:25,469 --> 00:12:27,275
I just wanted to talk
about the scene.

222
00:12:27,802 --> 00:12:30,001
Thank you.
I feel good about it.

223
00:12:31,172 --> 00:12:32,587
How do you feel you did?

224
00:12:33,328 --> 00:12:34,608
I felt good.
I just--

225
00:12:34,901 --> 00:12:36,901
- Good.
- I thought you were pretty good too.

226
00:12:37,021 --> 00:12:38,518
- Thank you.
- I did.

227
00:12:38,638 --> 00:12:40,315
- So I--
- You want a protein shake?

228
00:12:40,435 --> 00:12:43,015
You should have a protein shake.
Juice, get him a shake.

229
00:12:43,135 --> 00:12:44,667
Just give him the pads.

230
00:12:47,053 --> 00:12:49,053
- So it's about the--
- Put 'em on.

231
00:12:50,231 --> 00:12:52,216
I just wanted to talk
to you about the lines.

232
00:12:52,376 --> 00:12:53,828
Good ones, aren't they?

233
00:12:53,948 --> 00:12:55,428
A lot of 'em.
Come on.

234
00:13:02,590 --> 00:13:05,730
So if we--
It's really hot in here.

235
00:13:06,274 --> 00:13:07,370
Isn't it?

236
00:13:07,671 --> 00:13:10,082
You know how hot it can get
when wood combusts, don't you?

237
00:13:10,520 --> 00:13:11,671
3000°.

238
00:13:12,447 --> 00:13:13,455
Hot.

239
00:13:15,046 --> 00:13:18,099
I like to jack up the heat, acclimate
my body a little bit, you know?

240
00:13:18,682 --> 00:13:19,724
I'm good.

241
00:13:21,249 --> 00:13:23,660
- So--
