00:24:51,875 --> 00:24:55,700
Small literary shop servicing
over 65 working tv writers

489
00:24:55,820 --> 00:24:57,441
with less than five agents.

490
00:24:57,808 --> 00:25:00,458
- I like it.
- Grossed over $5 million last year.

491
00:25:00,578 --> 00:25:03,437
- I really like it. Which company?
- <i>Klein-Kuddler. You heard of them?</i>

492
00:25:03,557 --> 00:25:05,033
Is that Andrew Klein?

493
00:25:05,817 --> 00:25:08,403
- No go, the guy's a loser.
- No he's not.

494
00:25:08,523 --> 00:25:11,788
I'm not talking about what he makes.
I'm talking about his general essence.

495
00:25:12,126 --> 00:25:14,865
We need to project a certain image.

496
00:25:15,222 --> 00:25:17,419
And that washout
doesn't exactly fit the bill.

497
00:25:17,724 --> 00:25:19,838
And what do you project,
menopausal chic?

498
00:25:20,123 --> 00:25:23,216
He's not big agency material.
No go.

499
00:25:23,574 --> 00:25:25,957
I wasn't calling you
for your permission.

500
00:25:26,077 --> 00:25:28,180
Read your partnership
agreements then.

501
00:25:28,340 --> 00:25:30,432
Because my permission
is exactly what you need.

502
00:25:37,474 --> 00:25:39,377
- I thought you killed it today.
- Killed it?

503
00:25:39,497 --> 00:25:41,359
I was basically moving scenery.

504
00:25:41,519 --> 00:25:42,957
But at least you looked good.

505
00:25:43,077 --> 00:25:45,833
You got two big scenes coming up that
he's not in so you can make up for it.

506
00:25:45,953 --> 00:25:48,583
He'll probably jump out of a tree
and steal those lines too.

507
00:25:48,703 --> 00:25:50,458
We got a few more
tricks up our sleeves.

508
00:25:50,578 --> 00:25:52,431
Just say the word
and we'll have him in tears.

509
00:25:52,551 --> 00:25:54,122
I appreciate it.
Thanks.

510
00:25:54,242 --> 00:25:55,692
I hate to see you like this.

511
00:25:55,812 --> 00:25:57,918
- I'm sorry.
- I know what might cheer you up.

512
00:25:58,344 --> 00:26:01,046
I saw your favorite, banana cream pie,
over on the buffet table.

513
00:26:01,206 --> 00:26:03,253
- I grab you a slice.
- That would be nice, thanks.

514
00:26:03,373 --> 00:26:05,352
Slimy thief approaching at 3:00.

515
00:26:05,472 --> 00:26:07,020
Control yourself, Drama.

516
00:26:08,032 --> 00:26:09,221
Good work, Vince.

517
00:26:09,894 --> 00:26:11,374
- I try.
- See you tomorrow.

518
00:26:11,494 --> 00:26:13,408
Jason, I loved your work in <i>Narc</i>.

519
00:26:13,528 --> 00:26:15,891
Really really
inspirational stuff, man.

520
00:26:16,011 --> 00:26:18,028
- Really? Thanks,
- Take it easy.

521
00:26:18,632 --> 00:26:20,249
What the hell was that?

522
00:26:31,164 --> 00:26:32,661
Get a paper towel, will you?

523
00:26:39,420 --> 00:26:41,935
- Thought you were getting me pie.
- Got you a cookie.

524
00:26:42,055 --> 00:26:43,383
What about the pie?

525
00:26:43,651 --> 00:26:45,705
- Jason took it.
- What do you mean?

526
00:26:45,825 --> 00:26:48,632
I mean, I waited in line
and when I got to the pie

527
00:26:48,752 --> 00:26:50,508
he swooped in
and took the last piece.

528
00:26:50,628 --> 00:26:52,514
- And you let him?
- He's imposing.

529
00:26:52,634 --> 00:26:54,861
That's it.
Hey, Jason.

530
00:26:56,176 --> 00:26:58,920
- What's up, Vince?
- Did you take that pie from Turtle?

531
00:27:00,724 --> 00:27:02,315
Yeah, this guy.
My friend.

532
00:27:02,475 --> 00:27:04,926
He's waiting in line for this pie
and you took it.

533
00:27:05,046 --> 00:27:07,070
- I did?
- You kinda did.

534
00:27:07,615 --> 00:27:09,416
Oh, I'm sorry
about that, man.

535
00:27:09,536 --> 00:27:12,430
And while we're on the subject, you
kinda took a few of my lines today too.

536
00:27:12,550 --> 00:27:14,661
- Tell him, bro.
- What lines?

537
00:27:15,189 --> 00:27:16,260
All of them.

538
00:27:17,074 --> 00:27:19,046
I don't seem to be following
where we're going,

539
00:27:19,166 --> 00:27:21,156
but there seems to be
a bit of a problem here.

540
00:27:21,276 --> 00:27:24,646
The big monologue in the first scene,
advice to malone in the third scene.

541
00:27:24,766 --> 00:27:26,414
- Verner gave me those lines.
- Verner?

542
00:27:26,534 --> 00:27:28,254
Verner, our director.

543
00:27:29,330 --> 00:27:30,919
I assumed you knew that.

544
00:27:31,210 --> 00:27:33,238
- Well, I didn't,
- now you do.

545
00:27:33,474 --> 00:27:35,390
So why don't you go
take that up with him?

546
00:27:35,510 --> 00:27:38,446
Because any confusion that there
seems to be has nothing to do with me.

547
00:27:44,224 --> 00:27:48,528
I want to thank you, everybody,
for a fantastic first day.

548
00:27:49,416 --> 00:27:50,488
Auf uns!

